  "version": 1,
  "title": "Bell numbers modulo a prime are periodic with period (p^p−1)/(p−1) (Touchard, Hall)",
  "abstract": "For a prime p, B(n + (p^p − 1)/(p − 1)) ≡ B(n) (mod p) (Touchard 1933, Hall 1934, Williams 1945). The periods conjectured by G. C. Greubel in OEIS A146107, A146109, A146113, A146119 and A146121 (p = 17, 19, 23, 29, 31) are instances; OEIS already marks them correct. Minimality is not claimed.",
